  "result": "```json\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46705\"], \"answer\": \"This request has been filed before. Your text and screenshots were merged into PowerToys#46705, \\\"Dock: Add support for a band in the taskbar too\\\", which came from your earlier submission (#50930). It asks for the Command Palette Dock to be embedded in the taskbar as a band. A maintainer ([user]) said it is on the roadmap and that a prototype branch exists. Open edge cases include centered taskbars, display changes, Windows 10, vertical taskbars, and the Widgets button. Nothing has shipped yet, so there is no workaround for now. The Command Palette Dock itself is available from PowerToys 0.98 / CmdPal 0.9 and can be pinned to a screen edge next to the taskbar. Add your thoughts, such as the media peek or volume use case, as a comment on #46705 and follow it for updates. You don't need to open a new ticket.\"}\n```",
